       {
        "text": "In the present study, we used functional magnetic resonance imaging to explore which brain areas contribute uniquely to numeric computation."
       },
       {
        "text": "More importantly, the main effect of arithmetic complexity was observed in the left and right angular gyrus, while the main effect of rate of stimulus presentation was observed in the left insular/orbitofrontal cortex."
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
